<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Illyrian Revolt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6–9 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Bellum Batonianum, Pannonian–Dalmatian revolt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Illyrian Revolt was a rising of the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> against Roman rule from 6 to 9 CE. It began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> levied troops for a war against the Marcomanni and was led by two men named Bato, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daesitiates">Daesitiates</a> and of the Breuci. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> suppressed it after hard campaigns, and the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andetrium">Andetrium</a> in 9 CE ended the resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt.jpg" alt="Great Illyrian Revolt" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MaryroseB54 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Illyrian_Revolt_(English).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
